            <ArticleTitle>Nonpharmacologic Options for Treating Acute and Chronic Pain.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>S278-94</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1016/j.pmrj.2015.09.008</ELocationID>
            <ELocationID EIdType="pii" ValidYN="Y">S1934-1482(15)01015-1</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>This article provides a broad overview of the clinical nonpharmacologic treatment options for managing acute and chronic pain. Physical therapy and modalities, interventional techniques, emerging regenerative medicine, and cognitive behavioral paradigms of treatment are presented. Recommendations are evidence-based and are a practical resource for the musculoskeletal pain and sports medicine practitioner.</AbstractText>
